      "title": "Pair the possibilities",
      "text": "Each pea plant passes one of its two copies of a flower-color gene to a seed; each version is an **allele**. Here, P gives purple flowers even when paired with p, so P is dominant; only pp gives white flowers. A Punnett square pairs one possible allele from each parent in each box. For Pp × pp, half the boxes are Pp and half are pp, so each seed has a 1 in 2 chance of white flowers.",
